  "behaviorChanges": [
    "Default virtual rendering finishes loading after visible pages are rendered, prefetches nearby pages, and zeros/releases distant canvas buffers.",
    "Page navigation, zoom/fit, resizing, fullscreen and cancellation are connected to the public session API.",
    "Default virtual preview does not advertise complete-document printing. virtual:false retains eager rendering and that capability.",
    "Unopened page sizes use first-page estimates until PDF.js supplies actual page dimensions.",
    "The abort listener retains only its signal rather than the source descriptor. Viewport dimensions are read once before writing page sizes."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Same PDF.js engine before and after; this is scheduling engineering, not an independent parser/rendering algorithm or peer SOTA comparison.",
    "Loading settlement and the first nonwhite-content sample are distinct metrics. All final first-content ratio intervals overlap 1; no first-visible timing improvement is claimed.",
    "Canvas backing-store pixel counts do not measure total process, PDF.js worker or GPU memory. PDF.js retains its own document/page caches.",
    "The two 100-page fixtures are deterministic synthetic documents. The real repository document has three pages. Text search/selection layers remain unavailable."
  ],
  "conclusion": "Uniform 100-page load settlement: 1750.2 to 104.2 ms (16.80x); mixed-size 100-page load settlement: 1753.7 to 100.7 ms (17.42x). Initial canvases: 100 to 2; uniform canvas pixels: 27,000,000 to 540,000 (98% fewer). All 203 page pairs are pixel-identical. First visible content has no stable final change; no SOTA label."
